prompt:
Kreative Studio pose editor, animation part (STU-PE2). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Angles are degrees in every API. Coordinates are metres: +X is the figure's left, -Y its front, +Z up. Matrices are arrays of 9 numbers, row-major. Do not change the test file.

Write public/js/pose/bvh.js (NAME = bvh): export a clip as BVH motion-capture text that Blender imports. Get modules inside functions: V = need('vec', './vec.js'), S = need('skeleton', './skeleton.js') (JOINTS in parents-first order, byName; each joint {name, parent, rest, aim}), FK = need('fk', './fk.js') (local(name, e) -> 3x3 local rotation of a joint), A = need('anim', './anim.js') (sample(clip, t), frameTimes(clip)).

Axes: the Studio is Z-up with the figure facing -Y; BVH is Y-up facing +Z. yUp(p) = [p[0], p[2], -p[1]] for points; for a rotation matrix M, the BVH matrix is P * M * transpose(P) with P = [1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0] (row-major).

Export:
- yUp(p) as above.
- jointNames(hands): the names of S.JOINTS (in that order) whose aim is not null, leaving out finger joints (names matching /_(thumb|index|middle|ring|pinky)_/) unless hands is true.
- toBVH(clip, opts = {}): hands = !!opts.hands; names = jointNames(hands); returns a string.
  HIERARCHY: write the joints recursively, starting at 'pelvis' as ROOT; the children of a joint are the names in `names` whose S.byName[n].parent is that joint, in `names` order. Indent with two spaces per level. For each joint:
    ROOT pelvis / JOINT <name>
    {
      OFFSET x y z   (ROOT: 0 0 0; others: yUp(rest(joint) - rest(parent)))
      CHANNELS 6 Xposition Yposition Zposition Zrotation Xrotation Yrotation   (ROOT)
      CHANNELS 3 Zrotation Xrotation Yrotation   (others)
      ... the children ...
      End Site { OFFSET yUp(rest(aim) - rest(joint)) }   only when the joint's aim is NOT in names (write End Site, then {, OFFSET line, } on their own lines)
    }
  MOTION, then 'Frames: ' + times.length, then 'Frame Time: ' + (1 / clip.fps).toFixed(6), with times = A.frameTimes(clip).
  One line per time t: pose = A.sample(clip, t); first the three values of yUp(pose.root.pos), then for every name in `names` order: M = P * FK.local(name, pose.joints[name]) * transpose(P); e = V.matToEuler(M) (it decomposes M = Rz(side) * Rx(bend) * Ry(twist)); write e.side, e.bend, e.twist (that is Zrotation, Xrotation, Yrotation). Every number with toFixed(6), separated by one space. End the text with a newline.
